response.reasoning_text:
Bicg: s[j] reduction over i, q[i] reduction over j. Split into two loops: q loop parallel over i (row dot p), s loop parallel over j (column dot r). That's a standard transformation. Keep semantics (FP reassociation acceptable? s[j] sum order over i preserved if we loop i inner in same order — yes, keep i inner ascending). Write:

#pragma scop
for i: q[i]=0; for j: q[i]+=A[i][j]*p[j];
for j: s[j]=0; for i: s[j]+=r[i]*A[i][j];
#pragma endscop

with OpenMP parallel for on outer loops.

